EVALUATION.md §8.3, TYPES.md §12.1 (DECISIONS 226): a variant-level check shares every case's
check names: two variant-level checks of one name clash in the variant; a case's check named like a
variant-level one clashes in the case, reported at the later of the two in source.
-- teamboard/rewards.canon --
package teamboard

variant Reward {
  check positive: 1 == 1 else "a"

  item {
    count: Int

    check positive: count > 0 else "b"
    check wide: count < 9 else "c"
  }
  gold { amount: Int }

  check wide: 2 == 2 else "d"
  check capped: 3 == 3 else "e"
  check capped: 4 == 4 else "f"
}
-- findings.txt --
error[E5003]  teamboard/rewards.canon:9:11
  check name positive is used twice in Reward.item

error[E5003]  teamboard/rewards.canon:14:9
  check name wide is used twice in Reward.item

error[E5003]  teamboard/rewards.canon:16:9
  check name capped is used twice in Reward

3 errors, 0 warnings in 1 package (…)
